{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/identifier","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/time_zone_ptr-osvz"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/adjustTime(type:time:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/findInterval(type:time:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/getAbbreviation(interval:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/getIDentifier()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/getOffset(interval:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/isDst(interval:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/ref()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol\/unref()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"TimeZoneProtocol","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeZoneProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeZoneProtocol"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib16TimeZoneProtocolP","roleHeading":"Protocol"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/timezoneprotocol"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"TimeZoneProtocol","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"text":"PointerWrapper","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib14PointerWrapperP"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"GTimeZone","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct is refcounted and immutable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each time zone has an identifier (for example, ‘Europe\/London’) which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform dependent. See [ctor","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.TimeZone.new"},{"type":"text","text":"] for information on the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier formats. The identifier of a time zone can be retrieved using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.TimeZone.get_identifier"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A time zone contains a number of intervals. Each interval has an abbreviation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to describe it (for example, ‘PDT’), an offset to UTC and a flag indicating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"if the daylight savings time is in effect during that interval. A time zone","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always has at least one interval — interval 0. Note that interval abbreviations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are not the same as time zone identifiers (apart from ‘UTC’), and cannot be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passed to [ctor"},{"code":"GLib.TimeZone.new","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every UTC time is contained within exactly one interval, but a given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local time may be contained within zero, one or two intervals (due to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incontinuities associated with daylight savings time)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An interval may refer to a specific period of time (eg: the duration","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of daylight savings time during 2010) or it may refer to many periods","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"of time that share the same properties (eg: all periods of daylight","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"savings time).  It is also possible (usually for political reasons)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that some properties (like the abbreviation) change between intervals","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"without other properties changing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneProtocol","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol exposes the methods and properties of an underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GTimeZone"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"The default implementation of these can be found in the protocol extension below.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"For a concrete class that implements these methods and properties, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZone","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef"},{"type":"text","text":" as a lighweight, "},{"code":"unowned","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reference if you already have an instance you just want to use."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"GTimeZone","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" represents a time zone, at no par